{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import contextlib,copy,io,json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest import mock\nimport worksheet as w,verdict as v,paid_run as pr\nroot=next(Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/scratchpad/e2e/packet.p.json'\\\\'')).parent\ndry=root.parent/'\\\\''paid-dry2'\\\\''\nprint('\\\\''e2e files:'\\\\'',[p.name for p in root.iterdir() if p.suffix=='\\\\''.json'\\\\''])\np=json.loads((root/'\\\\''p.json'\\\\'').read_text());h=json.loads((root/'\\\\''h.json'\\\\'').read_text());g=json.loads((root/'\\\\''gains.json'\\\\'').read_text()); key=json.loads((root/'\\\\''key.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ndef verdict(p,h,g):\n data={f'\\\\''fake-{k}'\\\\'':json.dumps(x) for k,x in [('\\\\''p'\\\\'',p),('\\\\''h'\\\\'',h),('\\\\''g'\\\\'',g)]}\n real=Path.read_text\n def read(path,*a,**kw):\n  return data[str(path)] if str(path) in data else real(path,*a,**kw)\n with mock.patch.object(Path,'\\\\''read_text'\\\\'',read),contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n  return v.main(dry,'\\\\''fake-p'\\\\'','\\\\''fake-h'\\\\'','\\\\''fake-g'\\\\'',root/'\\\\''key.json'\\\\'')\nprint('\\\\''baseline complete synthetic'\\\\'',verdict(p,h,g))\ng1=copy.deepcopy(g)\ng1[0]['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''rule B material failure'\\\\'']=True\ndel g1[0]['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''reconciliation rests on it'\\\\'']\nprint('\\\\''material failure without causal review'\\\\'',verdict(p,h,g1))\nh1=copy.deepcopy(h)\nr=copy.deepcopy(next(r for r in h1 if r['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''H5'\\\\'' and r['\\\\''sequence'\\\\'']=='\\\\''linked-1'\\\\''))\nr['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''finding'\\\\'']='\\\\''material failure'\\\\''\nh1.append(r); h1.append(r)\nprint('\\\\''duplicate H5 failures on one key'\\\\'',verdict(p,h1,g))\nd='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\''\nreq='\\\\''Thesis v9 (NVDA)\\\\nLadder: Strongly bullish: Above \"'$400 billion.'\"\\\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 0 items]\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]\\\\n- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) total revenue: now rung 2, judged 2026-07-15\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: none\\\\n    The system\\\\'\\\\''s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): \"'$400 billion'\"\\\\n    Reasons (excerpt): about \"'$400B'\"\\\\n[Previous conclusion] none'\\\\''\nfor ref,case,q,r in [('\\\\''Analysts expect \"'$400B of Data Center revenue'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''ladder suppresses linked match'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect \"'$400B of Data Center revenue'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''corresponding positive, no ladder collision'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect 42 percent growth'\\\\'','\\\\''percentage-matching'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''\"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''42 percent'\\\\'').replace('\\\\''\"'$400B'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''42 percent'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect 400 billion dollars'\\\\'','\\\\''number written without \"'$'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''The company guides Data Center to \"'$393B'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''scope error without consensus keyword'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''Thesis v9\\\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 1 items]\\\\n- e1 [reported] Wall Street estimates the whole at \"'$393B'\"'\\\\''),\n('\\\\''No directly stated reference for Data Center.'\\\\'','\\\\''misattribution only in answer reasons, outside fixed dates'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\''))]:\n print(case,'\\\\'':'\\\\'',w.structural_flag(q,ref,r))\nc=pr.old2(); a=w.connect(pr.OLD2/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\nfor q,start in pr.pinned_plan('\\\\''1'\\\\'')['\\\\''readers'\\\\''].items():\n js=[j for j in w.judgements(c,q) if j[1]>=start]\n flagged={j[0]:w.structural_flag(q,j[4],w.request_text(a,j[5])) for j in js}\n ids={j[0] for day in w.FIXED_DATES for j in [w.in_force(js,day)] if j}\n print(q,len(js),'\\\\''structural'\\\\'',sum(bool(x) for x in flagged.values()),'\\\\''fixed'\\\\'',len(ids),'\\\\''union'\\\\'',len(ids|{i for i,flag in flagged.items() if flag}))\n if q=='\\\\''v9'\\\\'':\n  j=next(j for j in js if j[1]=='\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\'')\n  print('\\\\''old2 known 09-15 reference:'\\\\'',j[4],'\\\\''; selection:'\\\\'',flagged[j[0]])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -B -c 'import contextlib,copy,io,json,sqlite3\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom unittest import mock\nimport worksheet as w,verdict as v,paid_run as pr\nroot=next(Path('\\\\''/private/tmp/claude-501'\\\\'').glob('\\\\''**/scratchpad/e2e/packet.p.json'\\\\'')).parent\ndry=root.parent/'\\\\''paid-dry2'\\\\''\nprint('\\\\''e2e files:'\\\\'',[p.name for p in root.iterdir() if p.suffix=='\\\\''.json'\\\\''])\np=json.loads((root/'\\\\''p.json'\\\\'').read_text());h=json.loads((root/'\\\\''h.json'\\\\'').read_text());g=json.loads((root/'\\\\''gains.json'\\\\'').read_text()); key=json.loads((root/'\\\\''key.json'\\\\'').read_text())\ndef verdict(p,h,g):\n data={f'\\\\''fake-{k}'\\\\'':json.dumps(x) for k,x in [('\\\\''p'\\\\'',p),('\\\\''h'\\\\'',h),('\\\\''g'\\\\'',g)]}\n real=Path.read_text\n def read(path,*a,**kw):\n  return data[str(path)] if str(path) in data else real(path,*a,**kw)\n with mock.patch.object(Path,'\\\\''read_text'\\\\'',read),contextlib.redirect_stdout(io.StringIO()):\n  return v.main(dry,'\\\\''fake-p'\\\\'','\\\\''fake-h'\\\\'','\\\\''fake-g'\\\\'',root/'\\\\''key.json'\\\\'')\nprint('\\\\''baseline complete synthetic'\\\\'',verdict(p,h,g))\ng1=copy.deepcopy(g)\ng1[0]['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''rule B material failure'\\\\'']=True\ndel g1[0]['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''reconciliation rests on it'\\\\'']\nprint('\\\\''material failure without causal review'\\\\'',verdict(p,h,g1))\nh1=copy.deepcopy(h)\nr=copy.deepcopy(next(r for r in h1 if r['\\\\''part'\\\\'']=='\\\\''H5'\\\\'' and r['\\\\''sequence'\\\\'']=='\\\\''linked-1'\\\\''))\nr['\\\\''reader'\\\\'']['\\\\''finding'\\\\'']='\\\\''material failure'\\\\''\nh1.append(r); h1.append(r)\nprint('\\\\''duplicate H5 failures on one key'\\\\'',verdict(p,h1,g))\nd='\\\\''2026-07-15'\\\\''\nreq='\\\\''Thesis v9 (NVDA)\\\\nLadder: Strongly bullish: Above \"'$400 billion.'\"\\\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 0 items]\\\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]\\\\n- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) total revenue: now rung 2, judged 2026-07-15\\\\n    Comparison point stated by that judgement: none\\\\n    The system\\\\'\\\\''s forecast for it (our own judgement, not evidence): \"'$400 billion'\"\\\\n    Reasons (excerpt): about \"'$400B'\"\\\\n[Previous conclusion] none'\\\\''\nfor ref,case,q,r in [('\\\\''Analysts expect \"'$400B of Data Center revenue'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''ladder suppresses linked match'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect \"'$400B of Data Center revenue'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''corresponding positive, no ladder collision'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect 42 percent growth'\\\\'','\\\\''percentage-matching'\\\\'','\\\\''v21'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''\"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''42 percent'\\\\'').replace('\\\\''\"'$400B'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''42 percent'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''Analysts expect 400 billion dollars'\\\\'','\\\\''number written without \"'$'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\'')),\n('\\\\''The company guides Data Center to \"'$393B'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''scope error without consensus keyword'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'','\\\\''Thesis v9\\\\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 1 items]\\\\n- e1 [reported] Wall Street estimates the whole at \"'$393B'\"'\\\\''),\n('\\\\''No directly stated reference for Data Center.'\\\\'','\\\\''misattribution only in answer reasons, outside fixed dates'\\\\'','\\\\''v9'\\\\'',req.replace('\\\\''Above \"'$400 billion'\"'\\\\'','\\\\''Above \"'$450 billion'\"'\\\\''))]:\n print(case,'\\\\'':'\\\\'',w.structural_flag(q,ref,r))\nc=pr.old2(); a=w.connect(pr.OLD2/'\\\\''archive.sqlite'\\\\'')\nfor q,start in pr.pinned_plan('\\\\''1'\\\\'')['\\\\''readers'\\\\''].items():\n js=[j for j in w.judgements(c,q) if j[1]>=start]\n flagged={j[0]:w.structural_flag(q,j[4],w.request_text(a,j[5])) for j in js}\n ids={j[0] for day in w.FIXED_DATES for j in [w.in_force(js,day)] if j}\n print(q,len(js),'\\\\''structural'\\\\'',sum(bool(x) for x in flagged.values()),'\\\\''fixed'\\\\'',len(ids),'\\\\''union'\\\\'',len(ids|{i for i,flag in flagged.items() if flag}))\n if q=='\\\\''v9'\\\\'':\n  j=next(j for j in js if j[1]=='\\\\''2026-09-15'\\\\'')\n  print('\\\\''old2 known 09-15 reference:'\\\\'',j[4],'\\\\''; selection:'\\\\'',flagged[j[0]])\n'\"","aggregated_output":"e2e files: ['key.json', 'p-read.json', 'p.json', 'h.json', 'gains.json', 'packet.h.json', 'packet.p.json']\nbaseline complete synthetic ('pass', 'all three pairs improved')\nmaterial failure without causal review ('pass', 'all three pairs improved')\nduplicate H5 failures on one key ('fail', 'confirmed harm')\nladder suppresses linked match : None\ncorresponding positive, no ladder collision : own figure as market\npercentage-matching : None\nnumber written without $ : None\nscope error without consensus keyword : None\nmisattribution only in answer reasons, outside fixed dates : None\nv14 71 structural 13 fixed 7 union 17\nv9 70 structural 69 fixed 7 union 69\nold2 known 09-15 reference: Approximately $414 billion is the reference expectation, in rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). ; selection: own figure as market\nv16 56 structural 8 fixed 6 union 14\nv21 50 structural 0 fixed 6 union 6\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** The rebuild closes the round-29 rejected-summary and missing-packet paths. H3 still misses cases it is meant to guard, and I reproduced a pass with an incomplete gain review and a failure from duplicate H5 rows.\n\n### Round-29 fixes that hold\n\nThe paid gate now rejects a stopped or overrun ledger. The verdict requires all six summaries to be accepted for an ordinary comparison and handles a linked double refusal before requiring a worksheet. The P packet is separate and carries shuffled labels. The H packet includes the fixed-date reader answers, upstream requests, and the paired conclusion in force. The end-to-end checks demonstrate the earlier regressions, including H1’s three-versus-four refusal boundary. One earlier acceptance detail remains open: the gate infers completion from replay returning without an exception. Check the recorded completed calendar against the planned window. [Acceptance gate](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/paid_run.py:354) · [Verdict entry point](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:207) · [Worksheet packets](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:150) · [End-to-end results](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/e2e-checks.log:416)\n\n### Blocking findings\n\n1. **H3 uses the same selector in both arms, but the selector misses the specified harm.** I tested a v9 answer that presents the linked **$400B company forecast** as an analyst estimate for Data Center. The selector flags it until `$400B` also appears in the ladder. `sections()` puts the ladder in the same bucket as evidence, so a rung boundary suppresses the hit. The selector also misses a market claim made only in the reasons, a company estimate presented as segment guidance without the word *consensus*, and percentages such as v21’s growth reference. Separate actual evidence from prompt scaffolding, select market claims in the reference and reasons across the units these readers use, and exercise those cases outside the fixed dates. When a linked row has an error, require a finding on its paired control conclusion even if the selector missed that control row. An absent review currently counts as absence of the error. The dry run had **zero structural hits**, so its injected H3 finding tests verdict routing, not selection. [H3 specification](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:115) · [Selector](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:99) · [Paired H3 comparison](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:159) · [Dry selection count](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/e2e-checks.log:1)\n2. **Validate review records before counting them.** On the dry artifacts, I marked a gain’s supplying answer as a material Rule B failure and deleted `reconciliation rests on it`. The verdict still **passed**. Require an explicit finding on reliance whenever a material failure is marked. Also, the H-key set check collapses duplicate rows, but H5 counts the original list. I duplicated a single H5 failure and got **fail** for two failures. Reject duplicate review keys and bind P and gain reviews to the actual supplying judgement IDs in the stores. A quantified CPU correction also needs to be applied **per gain date**. The same corrected company forecast can be clear against one day’s segment forecast and definite against the next, while the current worksheet stores one adjusted class per company judgement. [H-row validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:221) · [H5 counting and gain validation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/verdict.py:170) · [Gain worksheet](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/worksheet.py:215)\n\n### Reading time\n\nI reproduced **90 structural hits** on old-2, rising to **106 distinct rows** once fixed dates are included. That projects **636 H3 rows** over six similar sequences before extra linked hits and paired-control follow-ups. I would budget **18–30 reviewer-hours** for the full protocol, separate from the roughly three-hour run. That assumes 20–30 seconds for each of the 864 dry-schedule P marks, 30–60 seconds per H3 trace at roughly 700 rows, and additional time for H4, both H5 reads, gain review, and adjudication. The design’s **8–12 hours** is too tight for that workload. Recount after fixing H3 and time a representative batch before sending. [H3 load](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/h3-load.log:1) · [Protocol workload](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PAID-DESIGN.md:141)\n\n**$7 remains a reasonable ceiling to propose once the blockers are fixed.**"}}
